Ghidra folded the two carry sources (3907 @e4fa, c40a/35a7 @e50d) to constants: the pristine renders the
`e511 jb 0xe4f7` empty-queue repaint break as `in_CF = 1; if (bVar5) break;` with bVar5 permanently false,
so the inner event loop NEVER breaks to OUTER on an empty queue -> 206f runs exactly ONCE -> the extender
per-frame op 0x0c is posted once and the mission never advances to a second frame.  It also never pumps the
INT-8 tick, so no timer/input event is ever queued (the tick's ISR runs only from fist_timer_pump).

Reconstruct faithfully (identical to the cc33 modal loop, patch 137, and the 459a modal loop, patch 242):
thread g_fist_cf for both poll sites (3907 and 35a7 return the x86 CF via the shim global -- patch 073) and
call fist_timer_pump() in the inner spin-wait.  Now the queue empties (or a frame event fires) -> c40a
returns CF=1 -> break -> OUTER 206f repaints -> op 0x0c re-posts (the intended per-frame iteration, once
459a's upstream render is un-blocked -- the c33c object-walk subsystem, docs/stage1.md).

Native<->wasm bit-identical (the cooperative pump is the shared __EMSCRIPTEN__ tick seam already used by
every modal loop).  verify stays 19/19.
